{"agent_run_ids": [], "applicability": [], "authority_tier": "community-reviewed", "claim_tier": "source_backed", "confidence": "high", "diagnosis_status": "source_supported", "diagnosis_summary": "Rock's public issue discussion and 16.6 source distinguish the unsubscribe link placed in a message footer from the email-client one-click control presented near message headers. The footer is a browser GET to Rock's preference experience, while one-click is carried in List-Unsubscribe headers and handled as a POST. Rock 16.3 release notes separately record one-click support, Email Preference Entry behavior for one-click requests, and the fix tracked by issue 5770. Issue 6040 itself was closed as clarification, not as a confirmed defect or fixed-version claim.", "enrichment_id": "rock_issue_enrichment:core-6040-one-click-unsubscribe-surface-v1", "issue_id": "rock_issue:SparkDevNetwork/Rock#6040", "issue_updated_at": "2024-10-16T20:18:54Z", "license_attestation": true, "redaction_attestation": true, "review_status": "approved_for_public_distillation", "reviewed_at": "2026-07-15T20:34:20Z", "reviewer": "briand-delegated-codex-review", "schema": "rock-kb-rock-issue-enrichment-v1", "source_path": "issues/communications/core-6040-one-click-unsubscribe-surface.json", "source_refs": ["https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6040", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6040#issuecomment-2417683447", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6040#issuecomment-2417837916", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/5770", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/blob/1.16.6/Rock/Communication/Medium/Email.cs#L35-L92", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/blob/1.16.6/Rock/Communication/EmailTransportComponent.cs#L966-L1063", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/blob/1.16.6/Rock.Blocks/Communication/EmailPreferenceEntry.cs#L262-L321", "https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8058", "https://www.rockrms.com/releasenotes", "rock_core_release_notes:44454c79b8cb0c37", "rock_core_release_notes:872a0d0f13553f9d", "rock_core_release_notes:01a3b88275961295"], "workaround_summaries": ["When validating one-click unsubscribe, inspect the delivered message's List-Unsubscribe and List-Unsubscribe-Post headers and the receiving email client's native control separately from the footer link. Do not make a browser GET auto-unsubscribe, because automated link scanners can issue GET requests."]}
{"agent_run_ids": [], "applicability": [{"assertion_id": "core-6081-fixed-by-commit-c90c1459", "assessed_at": "2026-07-15T20:34:20Z", "authority_tier": "official", "claim_tier": "source_backed", "component": "rock_core", "confidence": "high", "context": {"canonical_issue": "SparkDevNetwork/Rock#6064", "scope": "exact source revision for out-of-box next-generation check-in page security; release package inclusion requires verification"}, "evidence_refs": ["https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6081#issuecomment-2485973566", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6064", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6064#issuecomment-2485980271", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/commit/c90c1459fa4d428a7a15af9f76a23dfaac9517c7"], "fix_refs": ["https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6064", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/commit/c90c1459fa4d428a7a15af9f76a23dfaac9517c7"], "ranges": [], "status": "fixed", "version_scheme": "git", "versions": ["c90c1459fa4d428a7a15af9f76a23dfaac9517c7"]}], "authority_tier": "community-reviewed", "claim_tier": "source_backed", "confidence": "high", "diagnosis_status": "maintainer_confirmed", "diagnosis_summary": "A Rock maintainer closed issue 6081 as a duplicate of issue 6064. The linked fix migration adds ordered staff-role allows followed by an All Users deny so the out-of-box next-generation check-in security matches version 1 check-in, and issue 6064 is labeled confirmed and fixed in 16.7. Early alpha builds shared the same displayed file version before and after the commit, so exact build ancestry matters. Existing customized matching rules may not be overwritten and still require local verification.", "enrichment_id": "rock_issue_enrichment:core-6081-nextgen-checkin-duplicate-v1", "issue_id": "rock_issue:SparkDevNetwork/Rock#6081", "issue_updated_at": "2024-11-19T15:06:23Z", "license_attestation": true, "redaction_attestation": true, "review_status": "approved_for_public_distillation", "reviewed_at": "2026-07-15T20:34:20Z", "reviewer": "briand-delegated-codex-review", "schema": "rock-kb-rock-issue-enrichment-v1", "source_path": "issues/check-in/core-6081-nextgen-checkin-duplicate.json", "source_refs": ["https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6081", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6081#issuecomment-2485973566", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6064", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6064#issuecomment-2485980271", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/commit/c90c1459fa4d428a7a15af9f76a23dfaac9517c7", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/blob/c90c1459fa4d428a7a15af9f76a23dfaac9517c7/Rock.Migrations/Migrations/Version%2016.0/Version%201.16.7/202411182318196_UpdateNextGenCheckInDefaultSecurity.cs#L31-L71"], "workaround_summaries": ["Follow issue 6064 for the canonical resolution, use a build proven to descend from commit c90c1459fa4d428a7a15af9f76a23dfaac9517c7, and inspect effective ordered permissions on customized next-generation check-in pages."]}
{"agent_run_ids": [], "applicability": [{"assertion_id": "core-6917-affected-19.3.1-alpha", "assessed_at": "2026-07-15T20:34:20Z", "authority_tier": "source-code-confirmed", "claim_tier": "source_backed", "component": "rock_core", "confidence": "high", "context": {"scope": "stock classic themes containing query-stamped local Tabler CSS imports"}, "evidence_refs": ["https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6917", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/commit/1291dc2dd2f8bbf89596d3c812346a04bed041fe", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/releases/tag/19.3.1-alpha", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/commit/aae87fcb73df28c84caa91d3a1e7e390dc6059a7"], "fix_refs": [], "ranges": [], "release_track": "19.3", "status": "affected", "version_scheme": "rock_release", "versions": ["19.3.1-alpha"]}, {"assertion_id": "core-6917-fixed-by-commit-aae87fc", "assessed_at": "2026-07-15T20:34:20Z", "authority_tier": "source-code-confirmed", "claim_tier": "source_backed", "component": "rock_core", "confidence": "high", "context": {"scope": "exact source revision; release package inclusion remains unproven"}, "evidence_refs": ["https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6917", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/commit/aae87fcb73df28c84caa91d3a1e7e390dc6059a7"], "fix_refs": ["https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/commit/aae87fcb73df28c84caa91d3a1e7e390dc6059a7"], "ranges": [], "status": "fixed", "version_scheme": "git", "versions": ["aae87fcb73df28c84caa91d3a1e7e390dc6059a7"]}], "authority_tier": "community-reviewed", "claim_tier": "source_backed", "confidence": "high", "diagnosis_status": "source_supported", "diagnosis_summary": "The linked closing commit shows that CssProcessor passed the full CSS @import URL, including its query string, into filesystem path resolution. A preceding stock-theme change introduced query-stamped local Tabler CSS imports, and the public 19.3.1-alpha tag is the parent of the fix. The fix resolves the file with the query removed while preserving the original query when rebuilding the browser URL. Rock labels the issue for the 19.3 release line, but no later public package was available at review time to prove exact build inclusion.", "enrichment_id": "rock_issue_enrichment:core-6917-css-import-query-string-v1", "issue_id": "rock_issue:SparkDevNetwork/Rock#6917", "issue_updated_at": "2026-07-14T22:33:30Z", "license_attestation": true, "redaction_attestation": true, "review_status": "approved_for_public_distillation", "reviewed_at": "2026-07-15T20:34:20Z", "reviewer": "briand-delegated-codex-review", "schema": "rock-kb-rock-issue-enrichment-v1", "source_path": "issues/check-in/core-6917-css-import-query-string.json", "source_refs": ["https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6917", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/commit/1291dc2dd2f8bbf89596d3c812346a04bed041fe", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/releases/tag/19.3.1-alpha", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/compare/19.3.1-alpha...hotfix-19.3", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/commit/aae87fcb73df28c84caa91d3a1e7e390dc6059a7"], "workaround_summaries": ["Use a Rock build that contains commit aae87fcb73df28c84caa91d3a1e7e390dc6059a7, then verify a representative classic check-in page whose imported CSS URL includes a query string."]}
{"agent_run_ids": [], "applicability": [{"assertion_id": "core-6919-under-investigation-19.2.0", "assessed_at": "2026-07-15T20:34:20Z", "authority_tier": "source-code-confirmed", "claim_tier": "source_backed", "component": "rock_core", "confidence": "medium", "context": {"scope": "Azure-backed BinaryFile storage under concurrent first-use cache access; reported incident still requires reproduction"}, "evidence_refs": ["https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6919", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/blob/b4aee4df15d2aacf18d7c151e5601704ead7411b/Rock/Storage/Common/AzureBlobStorageClient.cs#L31-L80", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/blob/b4aee4df15d2aacf18d7c151e5601704ead7411b/Rock/Storage/Provider/AzureBlobStorage.cs#L131-L209", "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.collections.generic.dictionary-2?view=netframework-4.8.1#thread-safety"], "fix_refs": [], "ranges": [], "release_track": "19.2", "status": "under_investigation", "version_scheme": "rock_release", "versions": ["19.2.0"]}], "authority_tier": "community-reviewed", "claim_tier": "source_backed", "confidence": "medium", "diagnosis_status": "source_supported", "diagnosis_summary": "Public Rock 19.2 source uses a shared mutable Dictionary cache in the static AzureBlobStorageClient and performs a ContainsKey/Add sequence without visible synchronization. Microsoft documents that Dictionary requires caller synchronization when reads and writes can overlap. This supports a concurrency defect in the Azure-backed BinaryFile path, but it does not by itself prove that the reported 100 percent CPU incident or a specific call stack had this cause; the upstream issue remains open without a recorded fix.", "enrichment_id": "rock_issue_enrichment:core-6919-azure-container-cache-concurrency-v1", "issue_id": "rock_issue:SparkDevNetwork/Rock#6919", "issue_updated_at": "2026-07-14T19:15:18Z", "license_attestation": true, "redaction_attestation": true, "review_status": "approved_for_public_distillation", "reviewed_at": "2026-07-15T20:34:20Z", "reviewer": "briand-delegated-codex-review", "schema": "rock-kb-rock-issue-enrichment-v1", "source_path": "issues/hosting-infrastructure/core-6919-azure-container-cache-concurrency.json", "source_refs": ["https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/issues/6919", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/blob/b4aee4df15d2aacf18d7c151e5601704ead7411b/Rock/Storage/Common/AzureBlobStorageClient.cs#L31-L80", "https://github.com/SparkDevNetwork/Rock/blob/b4aee4df15d2aacf18d7c151e5601704ead7411b/Rock/Storage/Provider/AzureBlobStorage.cs#L131-L209", "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.collections.generic.dictionary-2?view=netframework-4.8.1#thread-safety"], "workaround_summaries": []}
